## UI Slice 2b-6 — Inline markdown rendering (live-preview, part 1)

The CodeMirror note editor now renders markdown formatting **inline** as you type: headings are larger/bold, `**bold**` is bold, `*italic*` is italic, `` `code` `` is monospace, and links/quotes/strikethrough are styled.

### What's in
- A CodeMirror 6 **`HighlightStyle`** in `useCodeMirrorEditor` mapping the markdown parser's highlight tags (`heading1–6`, `strong`, `emphasis`, `monospace`, `link`, `quote`, `strikethrough`) to **fixed `.cm-md-*` class names**, registered via `syntaxHighlighting(...)`.
- Matching style rules in the editor's theme (heading sizes/weights, bold/italic, mono code, accent links, muted quotes) — using only existing design tokens (`--primary`, `--muted-foreground`, `--font-mono`).

Fixed class names (rather than CM6's generated ones) make the styling directly testable — the test asserts `.cm-md-h1/-strong/-emphasis/-code` render for real markdown source.

### Honest scope boundary
This is the **rendering** half of live-preview. The raw syntax markers (`#`, `**`, `` ` ``) are still **shown** (just styled). Hiding them "at rest" when the cursor isn't on the line — true Obsidian-style live-preview — is the next increment (2b-7), a `ViewPlugin` + `Decoration.replace`. Deliberately split, not dropped.

### Dependencies
`@codemirror/language@6.12.4` + `@lezer/highlight@1.2.3` — already in the lockfile as transitive deps of `@codemirror/lang-markdown`, promoted to direct deps so they're importable. No new resolution, no lockfile churn.

